/*
  English strings of the macOS app.

  The keys are the Spanish text written in the Swift sources, so es.lproj needs no entries.
  Interpolations become placeholders in the key: text → %@, whole numbers → %lld, and a
  literal % in a key with placeholders becomes %%.

  To add a language, copy this folder to <code>.lproj (fr.lproj, pt-BR.lproj…), translate
  the values and keep the keys and placeholders as they are. Translate InfoPlist.strings too
  (the camera and microphone permission prompts). The build ships every .lproj in
  app/Resources, and the language appears in Settings by its own name.

  Check with `swift scripts/check-strings.swift` (also run by `make test`): it lists any key
  a translation is missing, since a missing key would show the Spanish text.
*/

